{"name":"Flashpoint","hex":"#f9f2d1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flashpoint","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of flash point."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flashpoint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flash point","blocks":[{"text":"The flash point of a material is the lowest temperature at which a liquid gives off enough vapor so that it will ignite in the presence of an ignition source. This is different from the fire point, which is the lowest temperature at which the vapors keep burning after the ignition source is removed. The fire point is higher than the flash point, because at the flash point the rate at which the vapor is produced is not sufficient to sustain combustion. The flash point is also sometimes confused with the autoignition temperature, the temperature that causes spontaneous ignition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Flaming_cocktails.jpg/330px-Flaming_cocktails.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flash_point","wikidata":"Q194376"},{"title":"Flashpoint (1972 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Flashpoint is a 1972 Australian film."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flashpoint_(1972_film)","wikidata":"Q5457663"},{"title":"Flashpoint (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Flashpoint\" is a 2011 comic book crossover story arc published by DC Comics. Consisting of an eponymous core limited series and a number of tie-in titles, the storyline premiered in May 2011. The core miniseries was written by Geoff Johns and pencilled by Andy Kubert. The series radically changes the status quo for the DC Universe, leading into the publisher's 2011 relaunch, The New 52."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Flashpoint_%28DC_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flashpoint_(comics)","wikidata":"Q2465328"},{"title":"Flashpoint (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Flashpoint is a Canadian police procedural television series created by Mark Ellis and Stephanie Morgenstern and starring Hugh Dillon, Amy Jo Johnson, David Paetkau, Sergio Di Zio, and Enrico Colantoni. It follows the members of a fictional police tactical unit facing elevated threats and extreme situations beyond regular police work. The series premiered on CTV in Canada on July 11, 2008. In the United States, the first three seasons and the first part of the fourth were aired on CBS from July 11, 2008, until August 19, 2011. The show then aired on Ion Television starting on October 18, 2011, with the eighth episode of the fourth season. The series was distributed worldwide by Alchemy Television and Tele München Group."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Flashpoint_Intertitle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flashpoint_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q1066334"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/APM-932hd-1.png/500px-APM-932hd-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/APM-932hd-1.png/1280px-APM-932hd-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/APM-932hd-1.png/500px-APM-932hd-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAPM-932hd-1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg/500px-DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg/1280px-DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg/500px-DEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADEF-TECH_Bharat_2026%2C_KTPO_Exhibition_and_Convention_Centre%2C_Bangalore_254.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Flashpoint_%28teaser%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Flashpoint_%28teaser%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Flashpoint teaser","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlashpoint_(teaser).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/Flashpoint_cast.jpg/250px-Flashpoint_cast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Flashpoint_cast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/24/Flashpoint_cast.jpg/250px-Flashpoint_cast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Original main cast members (L–R) Dillon, Johnson, Taylor, Colantoni, Di Zio, Hogan, and Cram. Hogan was replaced by David Paetkau, playing Sam Braddock (not pictured), after the first episode.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlashpoint_cast.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Beige Chromography","image":"https://upload